1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,424
This video shows the new INR Monitoring section in the patient summary.

2
00:00:05,124 --> 00:00:13,019
Patience asked to see the INR trend during a consultation, as in ACT 2.0, and the consultation form itself is left untouched.

3
00:00:14,619 --> 00:00:35,522
A clinician opens the patient summary of a patient on warfarin. The INR Monitoring section starts collapsed, and the patient banner already flags the latest INR. Show readings and Record INR sit together on the right of the header. The section still shows the indication, the INR target, the next INR due date and the warfarin dose.

4
00:00:37,259 --> 00:00:48,708
Show readings opens the chart, which fills the full width of the section. Green is the target, 2.0 to 3.0 here, orange is just outside it, and red is further out.

5
00:00:49,899 --> 00:00:59,572
Each reading in the table has a coloured dot and a word, in range, above target or below target, with its dose change beside it. Hide readings collapses the section again.

6
00:01:01,572 --> 00:01:08,505
To correct a reading, I open Show readings and click Edit on the latest row. The editor opens in a panel beside the summary.

7
00:01:10,572 --> 00:01:14,310
I change the INR value to 4.4 and press Save.

8
00:01:17,092 --> 00:01:23,454
The row now reads 4.4, above target, the chart point has moved, and the patient banner shows the new value.

9
00:01:25,454 --> 00:01:29,529
Now I start a consultation and type a sentence into Interval History.

10
00:01:36,214 --> 00:01:44,482
I click Record INR in the collapsed section. The INR form opens in its own window, and nothing asks me to discard the consultation.

11
00:01:45,574 --> 00:01:53,376
I choose the indication and the target, enter the date and an INR of 3.4, answer No to dose change, and press Save.

12
00:01:55,294 --> 00:02:02,144
The consultation window comes back with my sentence still in Interval History, and Show readings reveals the new reading.

13
00:02:04,144 --> 00:02:11,878
This patient's own target is 2.5 to 3.5. The chart keeps its standard bands and draws that target as a dashed box.

14
00:02:13,744 --> 00:02:21,035
When there are more than five readings, See all opens the INR reviews page, with the same full-width chart above its table.

15
00:02:23,035 --> 00:02:24,568
Two things are left for later.

16
00:02:25,268 --> 00:02:30,956
The agreed target range, ticket AR-124, is still open with the clinical lead.

17
00:02:31,656 --> 00:02:33,572
The Results tab is unchanged.
